       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.             SCODEUPD.
       AUTHOR.                 DAVID A. PLUM, JR.
       DATE-WRITTEN.           APRIL - MAY 1985.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.           THE GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER COMPANY.
      *REMARKS.
      **************************************************************
      *D  S C O D E U P D         CODE UPDATE SUBPROGRAM           *
      *                                                            *
      *   THIS SUBPROGRAM IS CALLED BY:                            *
      *       1) TDSCMAIN                                          *
      *                                                            *
      *   SUBPROGRAMS CALLED:                                      *
      *       1) CRFMTKWM - REFORMAT KEYWORD/MODIFIER SUBPROGRAM   *
      *       2) CRFMTMFR - REFORMAT MANUFACTURER SUBPROGRAM       *
      *       3) TPLTMAST - INPLANT DATA SUBPROGRAM                *
      * >>>-->4) TSCRPRT2 - SCREEN PRINT SUBPROGRAM *DELETED*      *
      *       5) TBLOWUP  - BLOWUP SUBPROGRAM                      *
      *       6) TDATECK2 - DATE SUBPROGRAM                        *
      *       7) SDSCTRNS - DESCRIPTION TRANSLATION SUBPROGRAM     *
      *       8) CCODECHK - CODE CHECK SUBPROGRAM                  *
      *       9) SCODEDEL - CODE DELETE SUBPROGRAM                 *
      *                                                            *
      **************************************************************
      *                                                            *
      *D  THIS SUBPROGRAM PERFORMS THE FOLLOWING FUNCTIONS:        *
      *D                                                           *
      *D      1) LOADING OF NEW CODES WITH THEIR KEYWORD/MODIFIER, *
      *D         MANUFACTURERS, MANUFACTURER'S PART NUMBERS,       *
      *D         DESCRIPTION, PRIMARY BIN LOCATION, AND INPLANT    *
      *D         DATA.  A KEYWORD/MODIFIER AND DESCRIPTION IN A    *
      *D         SECOND LANGUAGE CAN ALSO BE ADDED.                *
      *D                                                           *
      *D      2) MODIFYING CODE INFORMATION                        *
      *D         A) KEYWORD/MODIFIER AND/OR DESCRIPTION            *
      *D            (IN ONE AND/OR BOTH LANGUAGES)                 *
      *D         B) MANUFACTURERS AND MANUFACTURER'S PART NUMBERS  *
      *D         C) INPLANT DATA USING "TPLTMAST"                  *
      *D                                                           *
      *D      3) DELETION OF CODES FROM THE DATA BASE USING        *
      *D         "SCODEDEL"                                        *
      *                                                            *
      **************************************************************
      *   PROGRAM CHANGES:                                         *
      *                                                            *
      *   07/31/85  CHANGED PROGRAM AND SCREENS TO ALLOW ENTRY OF  *
      *             THE PRIMARY BIN LOACTION RATHER THAN THE       *
      *             PREVIOUS CODE.  VARIABLE NAMES WERE REVISED TO *
      *             REFLECT THIS CHANGE.      D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *   08/06/85  DATA BASE LOGGING CALLS WERE ADDED TO THIS     *
      *             PROGRAM.                  D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *  10/02/85 THE FOLLOWING PROGRAM CHANGES WERE MADE:         *
      *           1) CALLS TO THE SUBPROGRAM "TRSTRKWM" WERE       *
      *              REPLACED WITH CALLS TO "TRFMTKWM".  KEYWORDS  *
      *              AND MODIFIERS ARE NO LONGER LIMITED TO ONLY   *
      *              THREE WORDS.                                  *
      *           2) CALLS TO THE SUBPROGRAM "TRSTRMFR" WERE       *
      *              REPLACED WITH CALLS TO  "TRFMTMFR".           *
      *              MANUFACTURER NAMES ARE NO LONGER LIMITED TO   *
      *              ONLY SIX WORDS.                               *
      *           3) THE DATE CHECK SUBPROGRAM "TDATECK2" WILL NOW *
      *              BE CALLED IN PLACE OF "TDATECHK".             *
      *           4) CONVERTED PROGRAM TO MULTI-LANGUAGE           *
      *              CAPABILITY USING NSL CALLS.                   *
      *           5) THE SCREEN PRINT SUBPROGRAM "TSCRPRT2" WILL   *
      *              NOW BE CALLED INSTEAD OF "TSCRPRNT".          *
      *                                       D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *  10/08/85 THE FOLLOWING REVISIONS WERE MADE TO PROVIDE     *
      *           FOR THE USE A SECOND LANGUAGE:                   *
      *           1) CODE ADD FUNCTION:                            *
      *              A) PROVIDED FOR THE LINKING OF A SECOND KWM   *
      *                 TO A CODE (KWM IN SECOND LANGUAGE)         *
      *              B) PROVIDED FOR THE ADDITION OF A SECOND      *
      *                 DESCRIPTION FOR A CODE (SECOND LANGUAGE)   *
      *              C) REVISED THE POSITIONING OF DATA WITHIN     *
      *                 DDESC AND DDESC2.  KWM REMAINS IN 00 REC,  *
      *                 DESCRIPTION IS MOVED UP TO RECS 01 THRU 15,*
      *                 LOCAL DESC REMAINS IN REC 99, AND MFR INFO *
      *                 WILL NO LONGER BE STORED AS PART OF THE    *
      *                 DESCRIPTION.                               *
      *           2) MODIFY KWM AND/OR DESC FUNCTION:              *
      *              A) PROVIDED FOR THE MODIFICATION OF THE       *
      *                 SECOND LANGUAGE KWM AND/OR DESCRIPTION     *
      *              B) MADE THE NECESSARY REVISIONS TO HANDLE     *
      *                 THE NEW POSITIONING OF DATA WITHIN DDESC   *
      *                 AND DDESC2                                 *
      *           3) MODIFY MFR INFORMATION FUNCTION:              *
      *              A) REVISED LOGIC TO PLACE MFR INFORMATION IN  *
      *                 DMANPART ONLY                              *
      *           4) CODE DELETE FUNCTION:                         *
      *              A) PROVIDED FOR THE DELETION OF DATA IN       *
      *                 DDESC2 WHEN A CODE IS DELETED              *
      *                                       D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *  10/16/85 ADDED EDIT CHECKS TO INSURE THAT IF A 2ND        *
      *           LANGUAGE KWM IS ENTERED THAT IT IS NOT EQUAL TO  *
      *           THE KWM IN THE FIRST LANGUAGE.                   *
      *                                       D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *  01/14/86 THE FOLLOWING PROGRAM CHANGES WERE MADE:
      *           1) REMOVED THE EDIT CHECKS ADDED ON 10/16/85.    *
      *              THE KWM CAN BE THE SAME IN BOTH LANGUAGES.    *
      *           2) THE FOLLOWING CHANGES RELATED TO CORPORATE    *
      *              CODES VERSUS PLANT CODES WERE ADDED.  FOR     *
      *              PURPOSES OF THESE CHANGES CORPORATE AND PLANT *
      *              CODES ARE DEFINED AS FOLLOWS:                 *
      *                                                            *
      *              CORPORATE CODE - AN INTERPLANT CODE DEFINED   *
      *              TO THE CORPORATE DATABASE IN AKRON.           *
      *              CHARACTERS 5, 6 AND 7 OF THIS 7 CHARACTER     *
      *              CODE DO NOT CONTAIN ANY ALPHABETIC CHARACTERS *
      *              (A THRU Z).                                   *
      *                                                            *
      *              PLANT CODE - AN INTRAPLANT CODE WHICH IS NOT  *
      *              DEFINED TO THE CORPORATE DATABASE.  AT LEAST  *
      *              ONE OF THE LAST 3 CHARACTERS OF THIS 7        *
      *              CHARACTER CODE (BYTES 5 THRU 7) MUST CONTAIN  *
      *              AN ALPHABETIC CHARACTER.                      *
      *                                                            *
      *              A STAND-ALONE-PLANT DOES NOT FOLLOW THESE     *
      *              DEFINITIONS OF CORPORATE AND PLANT CODES,     *
      *              INSTEAD IT USES ANY 7 CHARACTER CODE AS A     *
      *              PLANT CODE (EVEN IF THE ITEM AND CODE MATCH   *
      *              AN EXISTING CORPORATE CODE EXACTLY).  BY      *
      *              DEFINITION A STAND-ALONE-PLANT IS NOT LINKED  *
      *              TO THE CORPORATE DATABASE (NO COMPUTER LINK)  *
      *              AND THEREFORE CONTROLS ALL OF ITS CODES AND   *
      *              THEIR DESCRIPTION(S) USING THIS SUBSYSTEM.    *
      *                                                            *
      *              A) CODE ADD FUNCTION:                         *
      *                 PROHIBITED FOR CORPORATE CODES.            *
      *              B) MODIFY KWM AND/OR DESC FUNCTION:           *
      *                 PROHIBITED THE MODIFICATION OF THE         *
      *                 AMERICAN LANGUAGE KWM AND DESC OF          *
      *                 CORPORATE CODES.                           *
      *              C) MODIFY MFR INFORMATION:                    *
      *                 PROHIBITED FOR CORPORATE CODES.            *
      *              D) CODE DELETE FUNCTION:                      *
      *                 PROHIBITED FOR CORPORATE CODES.            *
      *                                       D.A. PLUM            *
      *                                                            *
      *  02/06/86 CREATED SUBPROGRAM SDSCTRNS IN ORDER TO          *
      *           TRANSLATE/MODIFY THE DESCRIPTION IN DDESC        *
      *           AND DDESC2.                                      *
      *                                        A.M. KRAUSS         *
      *                                                            *
      *   03/24/86 CHANGED CALLS TO "TRFMTKWM" AND "TRFMTMFR" TO   *
      *            "CRFMTKWM" AND "CRFMTMFR" TO REFLECT THE CHANGE *
      *            IN SUBPROGRAM NAMING CONVENTIONS.               *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM                 *
      *                                                            *
      *  04/02/86  BROKE OUT THE CODE DELETION AREA INTO A         *
      *            SUBPROGRAM CALLED "SCODEDEL".  THE CODE DELETE  *
      *            CHECK FOR "CORPORATE CODE" WAS ELIMINATED.      *
      *            THE SUBPROG ALSO CREATES A "CODE DELETE"        *
      *            TRANSACTION 110 FOR EACH CODE DELETED.          *
      *                                  C.I.HILLES                *
      *                                                            *
      *  04/02/86  CHANGED THE FORMSFILE VDSCMAIN TO MAKE THE      *
      *            SECONDARY LANGUAGE KEYWORD/MODIFIER REQUIRED    *
      *            WHENEVER THE SECONDARY LANGUAGE FUNCTIONS ARE   *
      *            USED.  NO LOGIC CHANGES WITHIN THIS PROGRAM     *
      *            WERE MADE.  THE CURRENT LOGIC PROVIDES FOR THE  *
      *            BOTH THE PRESENCE AND THE ABSENCE OF A 2ND KWM, *
      *            SO NO PROGRAM CHANGES WOULD BE REQUIRED IF THIS *
      *            FIELD WAS CHANGED BACK TO BEING OPTIONAL.       *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM.                *
      *                                                            *
      *  04/03/86  ADDED ALTERNATE KEY LOGIC TO THE CODE ADD, AND  *
      *            MODIFY KEYWORD/MODIFIER AND/OR DESCRIPTION      *
      *            FUNCTIONS.  WHENEVER A NEW CODE IS ADDED WITH   *
      *            KEYWORD = "CODE" THE MODIFIER IS ADDED TO THE   *
      *            DATASET "MALTKEY" AS AN ALTERNATE KEY.  IN THE  *
      *            MODIFY KWM FUNCTION IF A KEYWORD IS CHANGED     *
      *            FROM OR TO "CODE" THE NECESSARY ADD AND/OR      *
      *            DELETE TO "MALTKEY" IS PERFORMED.               *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM.                *
      *                                                            *
      *  06/10/86  MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:                     *
      *            1) ADDED LOGIC TO THE ADD AND CHANGE MFR INFO   *
      *               ROUTINES TO PROCESS THE SELECTION FIELD      *
      *               WHICH WAS ADDED TO THESE SCREENS.            *
      *            2) CREATE A DDAILYTC RECORD FOR EACH CODE ADDED *
      *               TO MSTORERM.                                 *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM.                *
      *                                                            *
      *  09/04/86  REVISED THE DESCRIPTION ADD AND DESCRIPTION     *
      *            MODIFY ROUTINES TO BEGIN PUTTING DESCRIPTION    *
      *            TEXT INTO ID-NUM "09" RATHER THAN "01".         *
      *            THIS CHANGE WILL MAKE ALL PROGRAMS WHICH ADD    *
      *            DESCRIPTION TO DDESC AND/OR DDESC2 CONSISTENT.  *
      *            ID NUMBERS "01" THRU "08" ARE NOT BEING USED    *
      *            BY ANY PROGRAM AT THIS TIME.                    *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM.                *
      *                                                            *
      *  11/24/86  EXPANDED PRICE FIELDS FROM S9(6)V9(4) TO        *
      *            S9(11)V9(4).  ALSO ADJUSTED THE CODE ADD        *
      *            ROUTINE TO PROPERLY INITIALIZE ALL MSTORERM     *
      *            FIELDS UNDER THE NEW DATASET LAYOUT.            *
      *                                  D.A. PLUM                 *
      *                                                            *
      *C 10/07/93  JEFF BUNGO            REQUEST #6428             *
      *C           ADDED KSAM FILE KMANPART FOR MFR/PART/CC. WHEN  *
      *C           THE MANUFACTURER INFO CHANGES FOR A CODE, UPDATE*
      *C           THE KSAM FILE.                                  *
      *C                                                           *
      *C 04/05/94  BILL ROXBURY                                    *
      *C           PROGRAM CONVERTED TO AS/400 PLATFORM.           *
      *C                                                           *
      *C 10JUN1994       DAVE PLUM          REQUEST #6512          *
      *C    ADDED "UNLOCK" LOGIC FOR FILES DDESC AND DDESC2 AS     *
      *C    NEEDED TO PREVENT THE POSSIBILITY OF A RECORD          *
      *C    REMAINING LOCKED THROUGH A SCREEN.                     *
      *C                                                           *
      *C 13FEB1995       DAVE PLUM                                 *
      *C    REVISED THE START DDESC2 LOGIC FOUND IN PARAGRAPHS     *
      *C    624-RETRIEVE-DDESC2 AND 6252-REPLACE-DDESC2 TO HANDLE  *
      *C    THE CASE WHERE THERE IS NO SECOND LANGUAGE DESCRIPTION *
      *C    ON FILE WHEN THE USER ATTEMPTS TO MODIFY THIS          *
      *C    DESCRIPTION.                                           *
      *C                                                           *
      *C 15FEB1995       DAVE PLUM                                 *
      *C    REVISED SEVERAL IF STATEMENTS WHICH WERE USING THE     *
      *C    INVALID COMBINATION OF "NOT" AND "OR".  ABENDS WERE    *
      *C    OCCURRING IN CHILE BECAUSE OF SOME OF THESE.           *
      *C                                                           *
      *C 08AUG1995       CA YODER   REQ# 95-022                    *
      *C    ADDED LOGIC TO READ MPLTINFO TO OBTAIN A VALUE FOR     *
      *C    ESTIMATED LEAD TIME IF THE SWITCH IS SET TO YES.       *
      *C
      *C 09/12/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C   EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C   INCLUDE CENTURY FOR INIT AND ACTIVITY DATES.
      *C                                                           *
      *C   1/14/97    BILL ROXBURY REQ #95-012
      *C     UPDATE ENTRIES FROM NEW RECEIVING FILE (MCFLCSRCPT).
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C
      *C   19DEC1997     DAVE PLUM
      *C    RECOMPILED TO PICK REVISED "PLANTS" COPYLIB MEMBER.
      *C
